FEMA requires visual proof or proper documentation to validate damage. Common examples 
include: 
• Annotated maps; 
• Photographs; 
• Debris quantity calculation sheets; 
• Brief statements of percentage of work completed at the time of assessment; 
• Brief statements about whether work is force account, contract, or a combination 
thereof; 
• Labor cost summary; 
• Labor contracts and agreements;

